AB  - This research examines the effectiveness of AI-driven personalized learning solutions for university students with hearing impairments, addressing a significant gap in the existing literature regarding their engagement and learning outcomes. We explore the factors influencing the choices of students with hearing impairment to adopt these technologies, assess how AI enhances their interest in learning, and evaluate the overall educational experience provided by AI-driven platforms. Using a qualitative methodology, semi-structured interviews were conducted with students with hearing impairments and educators to gather in-depth insights. Data were analyzed using coding techniques, with a focus on interviewees' unique experiences. This research employed the 5Es Usability Model (effectiveness, efficiency, engagement, error tolerance, and ease of learning) to evaluate how well these AI platforms meet the specific learning needs of students with hearing impairment. The findings from this research aim to inform the development of more inclusive educational practices, ultimately enhancing students' educational experiences with hearing impairments.
