AB  - Detecting AI-generated scientific text is crucial to maintaining research integrity, trust, and evaluation. Existing methods struggle to generalize across binary and multi-class settings and to identify mixed human-AI content. To address these limitations, we propose Scientific Authorship Identification & Detection (SAID), a new approach that fuses handcrafted linguistic features with embedding-based semantic representations. SAID employs parallel branches to capture surface-level stylistic patterns and deep contextual semantics, which are fused at the feature level to enhance detection accuracy across binary and multi-class classification tasks. Extensive experiments are conducted on the AIGTxt dataset, evaluating SAID against baseline machine learning methods, deep learning approaches, and widely used commercial detection tools. SAID achieves binary classification F1-score improvements of 1.58-10.97% over baselines and demonstrates strong multi-class performance, particularly in detecting mixed texts. SAID achieved an improvement of 14.30% in accuracy compared to commercial tools. These results highlight SAID’s ability to reliably distinguish human-written, AI-generated, and mixed scientific content, providing a robust solution for modern authorship verification challenges.
